ev are vertical ionization energy/electron affinity (voltage-window proxies) 83	- Per candidate: gas-phase geometry optimization of neutral/cation/anion three times (r2SCAN-3c + OPT, automatic single point after optimization); spin multiplicity derived from electron count parity per charge state (even→singlet, odd→doublet); max 3 retries per molecule; CPU-slow (~2–3 hours per molecule), only at closing; forbidden inside the funnel 84	- Errors: 85	  - `ORCA binary not found; download academic Windows build from the ORCA forum` → install ORCA and add to PATH 86	  - `ORCA failed after 3 attempts for <smiles> (DFT not converged): ...` → honestly record "this candidate's DFT did not converge"; do not fabricate values 87	 88	## run-md — true MD diffusion endorsement (only closing Top-1) 89	 90	``` 91	bda run-md --box BOX [--engine ENGINE] [--t-ns T_NS] --out OUT 92	``` 93	 94	- Input `--box`: `{"molecules": {"EC": 60, "EMC": 40, "PF6": 10, "Li": 10}}` (Li ≥ 1; `t_ns` may be embedded; `--t-ns` default 10.0) 95	- `--engine`: `gromacs` (default) / `mace`. `mace` = ASE + MACE-MP Langevin NVT (fixed-seed box, 298.15 K, 1 fs step), requires only mace-torch, no GROMACS/.itp templates; for Top-1 cross-validation run both engines and compare D_Li_m2_s. 96	- Output: `{"D_Li_m2_s": f, "trajectory_ok": bool, "drift_check": "ok"|"drift"|"skipped", "achieved_density_g_cm3": f}` — on `trajectory_ok: false` (drift) record and report honestly (mace drift criterion = last-20% mean MACE potential energy drifting > 5% from the middle segment) 97	- Errors: 98	  - `unknown engine 'x'; legal: gromacs, mace` → fix engine name 99	  - `GROMACS not found; install via winget install GROMACS.GROMACS or conda` → install GROMACS (gromacs engine only) 100	  - `mace engine requires mace-torch; install via \`pip install mace-torch\`` → install mace-torch (mace engine only) 101	  - `box must contain at least 1 Li` → box needs ≥ 1 Li 102	  - `missing OPLS-AA .itp template(s): ...` → generate the corresponding .itp templates per the skill's `scripts/bda/simulators/data/opls/README.md` (gromacs engine only) 103	  - `gmx mdrun failed: ...` / `gmx trjconv failed: ...` → troubleshoot per trailing stderr content 104	 105	## render — HTML report 106	 107	``` 108	bda render --case-dir CASE_DIR [--out OUT] 109	``` 110	 111	- Reads `<case_dir>/log.jsonl` (entry 0 criteria + all action entries), produces a self-contained HTML (task overview / iteration trajectory / funnel statistics / stage results / true DFT-MD endorsement / final recommendation / design notes — seven sections), written to `<case_dir>/<out>` (default `report.html`) 112	- No log.jsonl → renders an empty report; no corresponding entry → section shows "no data yet" 113	- Errors: no custom validation; log-line JSON parse failure → traceback pointing at the line number 114	- Where used: last closing step; report content deterministically generated from log.jsonl, no extra LLM calls 115	 116	## run-comp — electrode composition screening (CHGNet periodic relaxation) 117	 118	``` 119	bda run-comp --in IN --out OUT 120	``` 121	 122	- **Environment requirement**: CUDA torch (GPU relaxation ~20 s/state); CPU torch relaxation does not converge (measured). Local `.venv` is CPU torch — use `D:/anaconda/envs/py312/python.exe -m bda run-comp ...` (py312 has chgnet/pymatgen/ase + torch 2.13.0+cu126) 123	- Input `--in`: `{"candidates": [{"formula": "Li(Ni0.7Mn0.05Co0.05Si0.1Mg0.1)O2", "name": "NMC-SiMg"}]}` — NMC811 lattice site substitution; TM fractions must sum to 1 124	- Output: `{"baseline": {NMC811 energy + Li metal reference}, "candidates": [{formula, realized_tm_counts, avg_voltage_v, capacity_mah_g, e_full_ev, e_delith_ev, converged, rel_stability_ev_atom}], "calibration_note"}` 125	- Definitions (stated honestly, written to the report): 126	  - Average voltage = −[E(Li_x2)−E(Li_x1)−n_removed·E_Li]/n_removed (x∈[0.3,1], includes Li metal reference; NMC811 self-calibration ≈3.82 vs literature 3.8 V) 127	  - Capacity = 0.